services:
  backend:
    ***REMOVED*** Example local overrides. Copy this file to compose.override.yml and edit
    ***REMOVED*** values that differ from your machine or workflow. compose.override.yml
    ***REMOVED*** is gitignored — machine-specific paths never get released.
    environment:
      TZ: ${TZ:-America/Toronto}
      ***REMOVED*** Uncomment and adjust if your planet file name differs from the
      ***REMOVED*** settings.py default (history-260209.osm.pbf):
      ***REMOVED*** PLANET_OSM_FILE_PATH: /app/data/OSM-PBF-FILES/planet/latest.osm.pbf
    ***REMOVED*** The most common override: bind your host data disks into the app.
    ***REMOVED*** volumes:
    ***REMOVED***   - /path/to/OSM-PBF-FILES:/app/data/OSM-PBF-FILES
    ***REMOVED***   - /path/to/osm_polygon_files:/app/data/osm_polygon_files

  worker:
    environment:
      TZ: ${TZ:-America/Toronto}
      ***REMOVED*** The base compose pins the worker to GPU 1 (the pipeline compute
      ***REMOVED*** card, see docker-compose.yml comments). Override only to move it
      ***REMOVED*** to another card, e.g. the idle RTX 2070:
      ***REMOVED*** NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES: "0"
    ***REMOVED*** Optional: GPU reservations via deploy (valid alongside runtime:
    ***REMOVED*** nvidia in docker-compose.yml). The backend itself does no GPU work —
    ***REMOVED*** GPU compute lives in worker / ollama / ollama-research.
    ***REMOVED*** deploy:
    ***REMOVED***   resources:
    ***REMOVED***     reservations:
    ***REMOVED***       devices:
    ***REMOVED***         - driver: nvidia
    ***REMOVED***           count: all
    ***REMOVED***           capabilities: [gpu]
